
<p>I don’t want to spoil any of this story from David Gelphman, which he wrote back in 2013, but which I only came across this week. Go read it. But before you do, one bit of context you should keep in mind is that the original iPad was <em>unveiled</em> at a special Apple event <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2010/01/27Apple-Launches-iPad/">on 27 January 2010</a>, but it didn’t <em>ship</em> until <a href="https://daringfireball.net/2010/04/the_ipad">early April</a>. Gelphman’s story takes place in that interregnum.</p>

